  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 219 PM MDT WED AUG 12 2026\nScattered showers and thunderstorms will continue into Saturday\nas moisture remains under persistent southwest flow aloft while\nanother shortwave rotates through the area. Precipitable water\nvalues will remain high (near the 80th to 90th percentile), so\nthe risk for localized flash flooding over recent burn scars\nacross central Idaho will persist through Saturday afternoon. A\nwarming and drying trend is expected to take hold Sunday and\nMonday as weak upper-level ridging attempts to build into the\nIntermountain West. Moisture will begin to scour out from west\nto east, though lingering low-level moisture will maintain a\nslight chance (10 to 20 percent) of afternoon showers and\nthunderstorms over higher terrain. Temperatures will recover\nback toward seasonal normals for early next week. Model guidance\nsuggests another Pacific trough approaching the northwest coast\nby midweek, which could reintroduce breezy conditions, a slight\ncooling trend, and increasing precipitation chances.",
